# Network Reconnaissance — Metasploitable 2

## Overview

This phase documents the initial reconnaissance performed against the
Metasploitable 2 virtual machine within the isolated Wazuh SOC home lab.

The objective was to identify:

- Host availability
- Open TCP ports
- Running services
- Service versions
- Potential attack surfaces

All reconnaissance was performed against the intentionally vulnerable
Metasploitable 2 system inside the isolated laboratory network.

## Lab Environment

| System | IP Address | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Kali Linux | 172.20.10.4 | SOC / Security Testing Platform |
| Metasploitable 2 | 172.20.10.2 | Vulnerable Target |
| Ubuntu Server | 172.20.10.5 | Monitored Endpoint |

## Connectivity Validation

Before performing reconnaissance, connectivity to the target was verified.

```bash
ping -c 4 172.20.10.2

4 packets transmitted
4 packets received
0% packet loss

This confirmed that the target was reachable from the Kali Linux
security testing platform.

# Nmap Service Discovery

The following Nmap command was used:
sudo nmap -sS -sV 172.20.10.2

# Scan Options

| Option | Purpose                   |
| ------ | ------------------------- |
| `-sS`  | TCP SYN scan              |
| `-sV`  | Service/version detection |

