# Initial Attack Surface Assessment

The reconnaissance identified multiple network services that may represent
potential attack surfaces.

Particularly notable services include:

- FTP
- Telnet
- SMB
- RSH/RLOGIN
- NFS
- Java RMI
- MySQL
- PostgreSQL
- VNC
- IRC
- Apache
- Apache Tomcat
- AJP13

Because Metasploitable 2 is intentionally vulnerable, these services will
be examined during subsequent controlled security testing.

No exploitation was performed during this reconnaissance phase.

# Security Objective

The objective of the next phase is to determine whether selected exposed
services contain exploitable weaknesses and whether Wazuh can detect
security-relevant activity generated during controlled testing.

